<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Home - Engineering Graphics</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --ink:#16344f; --ink-2:#2a5a86; --accent:#c96a2b; --accent-soft:#fbeee4;
    --line:#dfe5ec; --paper:#f4f6f9; --card:#ffffff; --muted:#6b7686;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  body{margin:0; background:var(--paper); color:#1c2833; font-family:"Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; line-height:1.5;}
  .wrap{max-width:1040px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 20px;}
  h2{color:var(--ink); font-size:1.3rem; margin:0 0 6px;}
  .lead{color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 18px;}
  section{padding:30px 0;}
  section + section{border-top:1px solid var(--line);}

  /* hero */
  .hero{display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr; gap:28px; align-items:center; padding-top:34px;}
  .kicker{font-size:.8rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--accent); margin:0 0 8px;}
  .hero h1{font-size:2.1rem; line-height:1.15; color:var(--ink); margin:0 0 12px;}
  .hero p{font-size:1.02rem; color:#3a4a5a; margin:0 0 22px;}
  .cta{display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .btn{display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; padding:11px 18px; border-radius:10px; font:700 .95rem/1 inherit; font-family:inherit;
    cursor:pointer; text-decoration:none; border:1px solid transparent;}
  .btn-primary{background:var(--accent); color:#fff;}
  .btn-primary:hover{background:#b35c22;}
  .btn-secondary{background:var(--card); color:var(--ink); border-color:var(--line);}
  .btn-secondary:hover{border-color:var(--ink-2);}
  .btn:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink-2); outline-offset:2px;}
  .hero-fig{background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:14px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(22,52,79,.06);}
  .hero-fig svg{display:block; width:100%; height:auto;}
  .hero-fig figcaption{font-size:.78rem; color:var(--muted); text-align:center; margin-top:6px;}

  /* cards */
  .grid{display:grid; gap:14px;}
  .topics{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));}
  .topic{background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:12px; padding:16px; text-align:left; font:inherit; color:inherit;
    cursor:pointer; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px; transition:border-color .15s, box-shadow .15s;}
  .topic:hover{border-color:var(--ink-2); box-shadow:0 3px 10px rgba(22,52,79,.08);}
  .topic:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink-2); outline-offset:2px;}
  .topic svg{width:34px; height:34px; color:var(--ink-2);}
  .topic b{color:var(--ink); font-size:1rem;}
  .topic span{font-size:.86rem; color:#4a5866;}
  .topic small{margin-top:auto; color:var(--accent); font-weight:700; font-size:.8rem;}

  .features{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr));}
  .feature{background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:12px; padding:14px 16px;}
  .feature b{display:block; color:var(--ink); margin-bottom:3px;}
  .feature span{font-size:.88rem; color:#4a5866;}

  /* how to use */
  .howto{display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto; gap:24px; align-items:start;}
  ol.steps{margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; counter-reset:s;}
  ol.steps li{counter-increment:s; position:relative; padding:0 0 12px 40px;}
  ol.steps li::before{content:counter(s); position:absolute; left:0; top:0; width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--ink); color:#fff; font-weight:700; font-size:.85rem; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;}
  ol.steps b{color:var(--ink);}
  .tour-box{background:var(--accent-soft); border:1px solid #f1d2bb; border-radius:12px; padding:18px; max-width:300px;}
  .tour-box p{margin:0 0 12px; font-size:.9rem; color:#4a3a2c;}

  /* optional accounts + usage summary */
  .track{display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,420px); gap:28px; align-items:start;}
  .opt{display:inline-block; vertical-align:middle; margin-left:6px; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px; background:#eef2f7;
    color:var(--muted); font-size:.72rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.04em; text-transform:uppercase;}
  .track .cta{margin-top:6px;}
  a.btn{text-decoration:none;}
  .note{font-size:.84rem; color:var(--muted); margin:12px 0 0;}
  .me{font-size:.9rem; color:#2c3e50; margin:0;}
  .usage{background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:14px; padding:16px 18px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(22,52,79,.06);}
  .usage h3{margin:0 0 12px; font-size:1rem; color:var(--ink);}
  .stats{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:10px; margin-bottom:16px;}
  .stat{background:var(--paper); border-radius:10px; padding:10px 12px;}
  .stat b{display:block; font-size:1.45rem; line-height:1.1; color:var(--ink); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
  .stat span{display:block; font-size:.8rem; color:#4a5866;}
  .stat small{display:block; font-size:.74rem; color:var(--muted);}
  .stat.wide{grid-column:1 / -1; display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .stat.wide b{font-size:1.7rem;}
  .bars h4{margin:0 0 8px; font-size:.84rem; color:var(--ink);}
  .bar{margin-bottom:9px;}
  .bar-top{display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:8px; font-size:.8rem; color:#2c3e50;}
  .bar-top em{font-style:normal; color:var(--muted); white-space:nowrap;}
  .bar-track{height:8px; border-radius:4px; background:#eef2f7; margin-top:3px; overflow:hidden;}
  .bar-fill{height:100%; border-radius:4px; background:var(--ink-2); min-width:2px;}
  .usage .note{margin-top:4px; font-size:.76rem;}

  [hidden]{display:none !important;}
  .about p{max-width:760px; color:#3a4a5a;}
  footer{text-align:center; padding:26px 0 30px; color:var(--muted); font-size:.85rem; border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
  footer a{color:var(--ink-2); font-weight:600; text-decoration:none;}

  @media (max-width:760px){
    .hero{grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:18px; padding-top:22px;}
    .hero h1{font-size:1.65rem;}
    .howto{grid-template-columns:1fr;}
    .tour-box{max-width:none;}
    .track{grid-template-columns:1fr;}
    section{padding:24px 0;}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Engineering Graphics &middot; Interactive Drawing Simulators</p>
      <h1>Learn to draw, one step at a time</h1>
      <p>88 standard Engineering Graphics problems, each drawn in front of you with a scale, compass and
         protractor &mdash; explained and read aloud step by step, just as it is drawn on a sheet in the drawing hall.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="how-btn">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 2.5v11l9-5.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          How to use (guided tour)
        </button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" type="button" data-topic="curves">Start with Engineering Curves</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-fig">
      <svg id="hero-svg" viewBox="0 0 360 150" role="img" aria-label="A circle rolling along a straight line, its point P tracing a cycloid">
        <line x1="8" y1="130" x2="352" y2="130" stroke="#16344f" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path id="cyc-full" fill="none" stroke="#c9d3de" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/>
        <path id="cyc-done" fill="none" stroke="#16344f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <circle id="roll" r="50" fill="none" stroke="#5b87ad" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line id="spoke" stroke="#5b87ad" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <circle id="hub" r="2.6" fill="#16344f"/>
        <circle id="pt" r="5" fill="#c96a2b"/>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>A cycloid: the path of a point on a circle that rolls along a straight line</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Choose a topic</h2>
    <p class="lead">Every topic has its own list of problems. Pick one, then follow the solution step by step.</p>
    <div class="grid topics">
      <button class="topic" type="button" data-topic="curves">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 28c2-9 5-14 9-14s5 5 5 5 1 5 5 5 7-5 9-14"/><path d="M3 30h28" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
        <b>Engineering Curves</b>
        <span>Ellipse, parabola and hyperbola by several methods; cycloid, involutes, helices and the Archimedean spiral.</span>
        <small>12 problems</small>
      </button>
      <button class="topic" type="button" data-topic="lines">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 17h30" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M8 13l18-10M8 21l18 6"/><circle cx="8" cy="13" r="1.8" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="8" cy="21" r="1.8" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
        <b>Projection of Lines</b>
        <span>Lines inclined to one or both planes: true length, true inclinations and traces, with the line shown in 3-D.</span>
        <small>17 problems</small>
      </button>
      <button class="topic" type="button" data-topic="orthographic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="14" height="11"/><rect x="4" y="20" width="14" height="11"/><rect x="22" y="3" width="8" height="11"/><path d="M1 17h32" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg>
        <b>Orthographic Projection</b>
        <span>Front, top and side views of blocks, brackets and solids in first-angle projection, including sectional views.</span>
        <small>19 problems</small>
      </button>
      <button class="topic" type="button" data-topic="isometric">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 3l12 7v14l-12 7-12-7V10z"/><path d="M5 10l12 7 12-7M17 17v14"/></svg>
        <b>Isometric View</b>
        <span>Isometric drawings from given views, with every circle drawn by the four-centre method.</span>
        <small>20 problems</small>
      </button>
      <button class="topic" type="button" data-topic="development">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="11" width="30" height="12"/><path d="M9.5 11v12M17 11v12M24.5 11v12"/><path d="M9.5 11l3.75-7 3.75 7" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
        <b>Development of Surfaces</b>
        <span>Lateral surfaces of prisms, pyramids, cylinders and cones, including cut and truncated solids.</span>
        <small>20 problems</small>
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="howto" id="how">
    <div>
      <h2>How to use</h2>
      <p class="lead">Five steps to any solution:</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><b>Choose a topic</b> from the tabs at the top of the page.</li>
        <li><b>Pick a problem</b> and click <em>Solve this problem</em>.</li>
        <li><b>Change the given data</b> if you like &mdash; the solution is redrawn for your numbers.</li>
        <li><b>Click Start drawing</b>, then <em>Next</em> for each step. <em>Previous</em> goes back; <em>Show all</em> shows the finished drawing.</li>
        <li><b>Zoom, pan or go full screen</b> to see the drawing closely, and set the drawing speed and voice to suit you.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <p><b>New here?</b> Take the guided tour. It opens a real problem &mdash; the cycloid &mdash; and a pointer shows you where to click, with every step explained aloud.</p>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="tour-btn-2">Start the guided tour</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Shown only once the account server is set up (EG_API_BASE in account.js) -->
  <section class="track" id="track" hidden>
    <div>
      <h2>Follow your students' progress <span class="opt">Optional</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The simulator never needs an account. Create one only if a faculty member wants to see how their students use it.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><b>Faculty sign up</b> with a Google account, or with an email and password, and enter their institute's name.</li>
        <li><b>Students sign up</b> the same way, then choose their institute and their faculty from the list.</li>
        <li><b>Students stay logged in while they practise.</b> The problems they open, the steps they reach and the time spent on each topic are recorded.</li>
        <li><b>Faculty open the Dashboard</b> to see, for each student, which problems were solved step by step and how long was spent on each topic.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="me" id="me-line" hidden></p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" id="acct-btn" href="account.html" target="_top">Create an account / Log in</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" id="dash-btn" href="dashboard.html" target="_top" hidden>Open the faculty dashboard</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Only a name, email address and institute are stored. Nothing is recorded for anyone who is not logged in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="usage" id="usage" aria-live="polite" hidden>
      <h3>Usage so far</h3>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat wide"><b id="u-users">0</b><span>registered users</span><small id="u-split"></small></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="u-inst">0</b><span>institutes</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="u-hours">0</b><span id="u-hours-l">hours of practice</span><small id="u-hours-split"></small></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="u-opened">0</b><span>problems opened</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="u-done">0</b><span>problems completed</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="u-anon">0</b><span>visits with no account</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bars">
        <h4>By topic: problems completed &middot; time spent (registered + anonymous)</h4>
        <div id="u-bars"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">"Problems opened/completed" counts logged-in students only (an anonymous visit can't be tied to a problem); time spent includes visitors with no account.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the simulator does</h2>
    <div class="grid features">
      <div class="feature"><b>Step by step</b><span>Every construction is broken into short steps. Go forward with Next, back with Previous, or jump to the finished drawing.</span></div>
      <div class="feature"><b>Real drawing instruments</b><span>Watch the scale, set-square, compass and protractor being used on screen, exactly as on a drawing sheet.</span></div>
      <div class="feature"><b>Every step read aloud</b><span>Each step is explained in words and spoken, so you can follow while you watch. Turn the voice off at any time.</span></div>
      <div class="feature"><b>Your own numbers</b><span>Change the given data and the whole solution is worked out again for the new values.</span></div>
      <div class="feature"><b>On any screen</b><span>Works on computers, tablets and phones, with zoom, pan and a full-screen mode for projectors.</span></div>
      <div class="feature"><b>See it in 3-D</b><span>For many problems, turn the solid round in 3-D to see where each view comes from.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about">
    <h2>About this simulator</h2>
    <p>Engineering Graphics &mdash; Interactive Drawing Simulators is a teaching aid for first-year engineering students
       and their teachers. Each of its 88 problems is solved the way it is drawn in the drawing hall: in first-angle
       projection, with every line placed by measurement or by projection, and each instrument shown as it is used.</p>
    <p>Use it to learn a construction before drawing it on paper, to revise before an examination, or on a projector in class.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<script src="account.js"></script>

<footer>
